["<aside class=\"callout why\" role=\"note\"><div class=\"callout-t\">Why it matters</div><p>Old military ammunition leaves salt in your rifle. Left overnight in Fraser Valley damp, salt turns into rust.</p></aside><figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Why corrosive ammunition rusts: old primers contain chlorate; firing leaves salt; the salt pulls water from the air; rust follows within hours. Water dissolves the salt; oil does not. Clean the same day.\">\n<rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#EEF1EA\"/>\n<text x=\"200.0\" y=\"26.0\" font-size=\"18\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Corrosive ammo in 4 boxes</text>\n<rect x=\"8.0\" y=\"90.0\" width=\"88.0\" height=\"80.0\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#FFFFFF\" stroke=\"#1F3D2B\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"52.0\" y=\"124.0\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#17201A\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Primer</text><text x=\"52.0\" y=\"146.0\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#17201A\" text-anchor=\"middle\">chlorate</text><line x1=\"96.0\" y1=\"130.0\" x2=\"100.0\" y2=\"130.0\" stroke=\"#FF6A13\" stroke-width=\"3\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><polygon points=\"106.0,130.0 95.2,135.2 95.2,124.8\" fill=\"#FF6A13\" stroke=\"#FF6A13\" stroke-width=\"1\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/><rect x=\"106.0\" y=\"90.0\" width=\"88.0\" height=\"80.0\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#FFFFFF\" stroke=\"#1F3D2B\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"150.0\" y=\"124.0\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#17201A\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Fired</text><text x=\"150.0\" y=\"146.0\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#17201A\" text-anchor=\"middle\">leaves salt</text><line x1=\"194.0\" y1=\"130.0\" x2=\"198.0\" y2=\"130.0\" stroke=\"#FF6A13\" stroke-width=\"3\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><polygon points=\"204.0,130.0 193.2,135.2 193.2,124.8\" fill=\"#FF6A13\" stroke=\"#FF6A13\" stroke-width=\"1\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/><rect x=\"204.0\" y=\"90.0\" width=\"88.0\" height=\"80.0\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#FFFFFF\" stroke=\"#1F3D2B\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"248.0\" y=\"124.0\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#17201A\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Salt</text><text x=\"248.0\" y=\"146.0\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#17201A\" text-anchor=\"middle\">pulls water</text><line x1=\"292.0\" y1=\"130.0\" x2=\"296.0\" y2=\"130.0\" stroke=\"#FF6A13\" stroke-width=\"3\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><polygon points=\"302.0,130.0 291.2,135.2 291.2,124.8\" fill=\"#FF6A13\" stroke=\"#FF6A13\" stroke-width=\"1\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/><rect x=\"302.0\" y=\"90.0\" width=\"88.0\" height=\"80.0\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#FFFFFF\" stroke=\"#FF6A13\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"346.0\" y=\"124.0\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#17201A\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Rust</text><text x=\"346.0\" y=\"146.0\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#17201A\" text-anchor=\"middle\">in hours</text><text x=\"200.0\" y=\"214.0\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#17201A\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Water dissolves the salt. Oil does not.</text><text x=\"200.0\" y=\"238.0\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#17201A\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Clean the same day you shoot it.</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>Corrosive primers leave salt after firing <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">65%</span>.</li><li>Salt pulls water from the air. Water plus steel is rust <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">65%</span>.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: the chemistry</summary><ul><li>Many older military primers use potassium chlorate. Fired, it becomes potassium chloride, a salt (65%, AccurateShooter, \"Coping with Corrosive Ammo\", 3 March 2018).</li><li>The salt attracts moisture; with oxygen it rusts and pits steel <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">65%</span>.</li><li>Oil alone does not remove salt. Water dissolves it <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">65%</span>.</li><li>Your bore is likely chrome lined, which resists this rust (70%, Wikipedia \"SKS\"). The gas tube, piston, bolt face and carrier still rust (Tip).</li><li>Most SKS ammunition sold in Canada today is non corrosive. Old surplus is the risk (Tip).</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Telling surplus ammunition: a steel cased full metal jacket surplus round and a brass cased soft point hunting round. A fired case with two flash holes inside (Berdan priming) is a surplus sign. If unknown, treat it as corrosive.\">\n<rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#EEF1EA\"/>\n<text x=\"200.0\" y=\"26.0\" font-size=\"18\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Spot surplus ammo</text>\n<rect x=\"40.0\" y=\"67.0\" width=\"88.4\" height=\"26.0\" rx=\"1.5\" fill=\"#7E8580\" stroke=\"#17201A\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><line x1=\"43.0\" y1=\"67.0\" x2=\"43.0\" y2=\"93.0\" stroke=\"#17201A\" stroke-width=\"1\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><path d=\"M128.4 69.1 Q163.5 72.2 170.0 80.0 Q163.5 87.8 128.4 90.9 Z\" fill=\"#B87333\" stroke=\"#17201A\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><text x=\"190.0\" y=\"85.0\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#17201A\" text-anchor=\"start\">Steel case, surplus FMJ</text><rect x=\"40.0\" y=\"117.0\" width=\"88.4\" height=\"26.0\" rx=\"1.5\" fill=\"#C9A227\" stroke=\"#17201A\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><line x1=\"43.0\" y1=\"117.0\" x2=\"43.0\" y2=\"143.0\" stroke=\"#17201A\" stroke-width=\"1\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><path d=\"M128.4 119.1 Q163.5 122.2 170.0 130.0 Q163.5 137.8 128.4 140.9 Z\" fill=\"#B87333\" stroke=\"#17201A\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><path d=\"M157.0 125.3 Q168.7 130.0 157.0 134.7\" fill=\"#9AA0A6\" stroke=\"#17201A\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"190.0\" y=\"135.0\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#17201A\" text-anchor=\"start\">Brass case, soft point</text><circle cx=\"100.0\" cy=\"210.0\" r=\"34.0\" fill=\"#7E8580\" stroke=\"#17201A\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><circle cx=\"92.0\" cy=\"210.0\" r=\"5.0\" fill=\"#2A2F2B\" stroke=\"#17201A\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><circle cx=\"108.0\" cy=\"210.0\" r=\"5.0\" fill=\"#2A2F2B\" stroke=\"#17201A\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"150.0\" y=\"204.0\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#17201A\" text-anchor=\"start\">Inside: 2 flash holes</text><text x=\"150.0\" y=\"224.0\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#17201A\" text-anchor=\"start\">(Berdan). Surplus sign.</text><text x=\"200.0\" y=\"280.0\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#FF6A13\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Unknown? Treat it as corrosive.</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>Steel case, sealed tins, military headstamp: think surplus (Tip).</li><li>Unknown? Treat it as corrosive (Tip).</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: how to tell, honestly</summary><ul><li>No outside mark proves a round is corrosive or not (Tip).</li><li>Signs of old military surplus: sealed metal tins, steel cases, Berdan primers (two small flash holes inside a fired case), military headstamps with a year code (Tip, common surplus guides).</li><li>New factory boxes usually say \"non corrosive\" on the box (Tip). Read it.</li><li>Rule: if you cannot tell, clean as if it was corrosive. It costs 10 minutes (Tip).</li></ul></details>","<aside class=\"callout warn\" role=\"note\"><div class=\"callout-t\">Warning</div><p>Study aid only. The official regulations are the law.</p></aside><figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Two bullets. Left, full metal jacket (FMJ): stays narrow after impact, red cross. Right, soft point: opens up, green tick. FMJ is illegal for hunting in BC.\">\n<rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#EEF1EA\"/>\n<text x=\"110.0\" y=\"60.0\" font-size=\"17\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#B3261E\" text-anchor=\"middle\">FMJ</text><text x=\"300.0\" y=\"60.0\" font-size=\"17\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2E7D4F\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Soft point</text><rect x=\"40.0\" y=\"86.0\" width=\"95.2\" height=\"28.0\" rx=\"1.5\" fill=\"#C9A227\" stroke=\"#17201A\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><line x1=\"43.0\" y1=\"86.0\" x2=\"43.0\" y2=\"114.0\" stroke=\"#17201A\" stroke-width=\"1\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><path d=\"M135.2 88.2 Q173.0 91.6 180.0 100.0 Q173.0 108.4 135.2 111.8 Z\" fill=\"#B87333\" stroke=\"#17201A\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><rect x=\"230.0\" y=\"86.0\" width=\"95.2\" height=\"28.0\" rx=\"1.5\" fill=\"#C9A227\" stroke=\"#17201A\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><line x1=\"233.0\" y1=\"86.0\" x2=\"233.0\" y2=\"114.0\" stroke=\"#17201A\" stroke-width=\"1\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><path d=\"M325.2 88.2 Q363.0 91.6 370.0 100.0 Q363.0 108.4 325.2 111.8 Z\" fill=\"#B87333\" stroke=\"#17201A\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><path d=\"M356.0 95.0 Q368.6 100.0 356.0 105.0\" fill=\"#9AA0A6\" stroke=\"#17201A\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><polygon points=\"80.0,160.0 140.0,160.0 150.0,170.0 140.0,180.0 80.0,180.0\" fill=\"#B87333\" stroke=\"#17201A\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/><path d=\"M260 170 Q280 146 300 160 Q320 146 345 170 Q320 194 300 180 Q280 194 260 170 Z\" fill=\"#B87333\" stroke=\"#17201A\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"110.0\" y=\"210.0\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#17201A\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Stays narrow</text><text x=\"300.0\" y=\"210.0\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#17201A\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Opens up</text><circle cx=\"110.0\" cy=\"244.0\" r=\"11.0\" fill=\"#B3261E\" stroke=\"#FFFFFF\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><line x1=\"105.5\" y1=\"239.5\" x2=\"114.5\" y2=\"248.5\" stroke=\"#FFFFFF\" stroke-width=\"2.5\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><line x1=\"114.5\" y1=\"239.5\" x2=\"105.5\" y2=\"248.5\" stroke=\"#FFFFFF\" stroke-width=\"2.5\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><circle cx=\"300.0\" cy=\"244.0\" r=\"11.0\" fill=\"#2E7D4F\" stroke=\"#FFFFFF\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><path d=\"M295.0 244.0 l4.0 4.0 l7.0 -8.0\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#FFFFFF\" stroke-width=\"2.5\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><text x=\"200.0\" y=\"284.0\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#B3261E\" text-anchor=\"middle\">FMJ is illegal for hunting in BC.</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>Surplus rounds are almost all full metal jacket (Tip).</li><li><button class=\"term\" data-term=\"Full metal jacket\">Full metal jacket</button> bullets are illegal for hunting in BC (British Columbia) <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">99%</span>.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: the law</summary><aside class=\"callout law\" role=\"note\"><div class=\"callout-t\">BC Hunting and Trapping Regulations Synopsis, page 12</div><p>\"It is unlawful to hunt or trap with a rifle using a full metal jacketed non-expanding bullet, or a tracer, incendiary, or explosive bullet.\"</p></aside><ul><li>Use surplus only for practice at the range. Hunt with a soft point or other expanding bullet (99%, <a href=\"#/s/rb-legal-methods/0\">Rule Book: legal methods</a>).</li><li>Keep range ammunition and hunting ammunition in different boxes, and only hunting rounds in your hunting bag (Tip).</li></ul></details>","<p>Point in a safe direction. Finger off the trigger. Unloaded and proved. Field stripped (<a href=\"#/s/mc-sks-06\">chapter 6</a>).</p><div class=\"steps\" data-n=\"4\"><div class=\"steps-head\"><b>Clean after corrosive ammunition in 4 steps</b><span class=\"steps-count\">1 of 4</span></div><div class=\"steps-track\"><figure class=\"step-frame\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Cleaning step 1: the bore. A rod with a brush runs back and forth through the barrel. Wet patches first with a water based cleaner, brush several passes, then dry patches until they come out clean.\">\n<rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#EEF1EA\"/>\n<circle cx=\"26.0\" cy=\"22.0\" r=\"13\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\" stroke=\"#FFFFFF\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"26.0\" y=\"27.0\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#FFFFFF\" text-anchor=\"middle\">1</text><text x=\"46.0\" y=\"28.0\" font-size=\"17\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\" text-anchor=\"start\">Bore: wet, brush, dry</text><rect x=\"40.0\" y=\"110.0\" width=\"320.0\" height=\"18.0\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#3A403C\" stroke=\"#17201A\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><line x1=\"10.0\" y1=\"119.0\" x2=\"300.0\" y2=\"119.0\" stroke=\"#8E9690\" stroke-width=\"4\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><rect x=\"290.0\" y=\"112.0\" width=\"30.0\" height=\"14.0\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#C9A227\" stroke=\"#17201A\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><line x1=\"120.0\" y1=\"90.0\" x2=\"254.0\" y2=\"90.0\" stroke=\"#FF6A13\" stroke-width=\"3\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><polygon points=\"260.0,90.0 249.2,95.2 249.2,84.8\" fill=\"#FF6A13\" stroke=\"#FF6A13\" stroke-width=\"1\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/><line x1=\"260.0\" y1=\"150.0\" x2=\"126.0\" y2=\"150.0\" stroke=\"#FF6A13\" stroke-width=\"3\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><polygon points=\"120.0,150.0 130.8,144.8 130.8,155.2\" fill=\"#FF6A13\" stroke=\"#FF6A13\" stroke-width=\"1\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/><text x=\"200.0\" y=\"196.0\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#17201A\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Wet patches first: water based cleaner.</text><text x=\"200.0\" y=\"218.0\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#17201A\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Brush several passes. Dry patches</text><text x=\"200.0\" y=\"238.0\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#17201A\" text-anchor=\"middle\">until they come out clean.</text>\n</svg>\n<figcaption><b>1.</b> Bore: wet patches, brush, dry patches.</figcaption></figure><figure class=\"step-frame\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Cleaning step 2: the bolt and the bolt carrier side by side. Scrub the bolt face, extractor and inside of the carrier with a wet toothbrush.\">\n<rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#EEF1EA\"/>\n<circle cx=\"26.0\" cy=\"22.0\" r=\"13\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\" stroke=\"#FFFFFF\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"26.0\" y=\"27.0\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#FFFFFF\" text-anchor=\"middle\">2</text><text x=\"46.0\" y=\"28.0\" font-size=\"17\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\" text-anchor=\"start\">Bolt face and carrier</text><polygon points=\"60.0,100.4 74.0,90.0 220.0,90.0 220.0,131.6 60.0,131.6\" fill=\"#D9DCD7\" stroke=\"#17201A\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/><line x1=\"64.0\" y1=\"112.9\" x2=\"216.0\" y2=\"112.9\" stroke=\"#17201A\" stroke-width=\"3\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-dasharray=\"7 4\"/><rect x=\"198.0\" y=\"125.6\" width=\"20.0\" height=\"7.0\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#59625C\" stroke=\"#17201A\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><rect x=\"230.0\" y=\"80.0\" width=\"130.0\" height=\"26.0\" rx=\"3\" fill=\"#C8CCC6\" stroke=\"#17201A\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><rect x=\"334.0\" y=\"74.0\" width=\"18.0\" height=\"8.0\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#59625C\" stroke=\"#17201A\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><line x1=\"330.0\" y1=\"106.0\" x2=\"330.0\" y2=\"120.0\" stroke=\"#3A403C\" stroke-width=\"4\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><circle cx=\"330.0\" cy=\"126.0\" r=\"9.0\" fill=\"#C8CCC6\" stroke=\"#17201A\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"200.0\" y=\"210.0\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#17201A\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Scrub with a wet toothbrush.</text><text x=\"200.0\" y=\"232.0\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#17201A\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Bolt face, extractor, carrier inside.</text>\n</svg>\n<figcaption><b>2.</b> Bolt face and carrier: wet and scrub.</figcaption></figure><figure class=\"step-frame\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Cleaning step 3: the gas tube and gas piston. They get the most carbon. Wet, scrub, dry and oil them.\">\n<rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#EEF1EA\"/>\n<circle cx=\"26.0\" cy=\"22.0\" r=\"13\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\" stroke=\"#FFFFFF\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"26.0\" y=\"27.0\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#FFFFFF\" text-anchor=\"middle\">3</text><text x=\"46.0\" y=\"28.0\" font-size=\"17\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\" text-anchor=\"start\">Gas piston and gas tube</text><rect x=\"40.0\" y=\"82.0\" width=\"320.0\" height=\"12.0\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#59625C\" stroke=\"#17201A\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><rect x=\"44.0\" y=\"76.0\" width=\"256.0\" height=\"15.0\" rx=\"3\" fill=\"#A8743F\" stroke=\"#6E4A2A\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><rect x=\"354.0\" y=\"79.0\" width=\"10.0\" height=\"18.0\" rx=\"2\" fill=\"#59625C\" stroke=\"#17201A\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><rect x=\"60.0\" y=\"147.0\" width=\"274.0\" height=\"6.0\" rx=\"2\" fill=\"#8E9690\" stroke=\"#17201A\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><rect x=\"332.0\" y=\"143.0\" width=\"18.0\" height=\"14.0\" rx=\"2\" fill=\"#8E9690\" stroke=\"#17201A\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><text x=\"200.0\" y=\"210.0\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#17201A\" text-anchor=\"middle\">The tube and piston get the most</text><text x=\"200.0\" y=\"230.0\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#17201A\" text-anchor=\"middle\">carbon. Wet, scrub, dry, oil.</text>\n</svg>\n<figcaption><b>3.</b> Gas tube and piston: wet and scrub.</figcaption></figure><figure class=\"step-frame\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Cleaning step 4: dry everything (bore, bolt, carrier, piston, tube), then a light coat of oil. Water left inside rusts too. Run a patch again over the next days.\">\n<rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#EEF1EA\"/>\n<circle cx=\"26.0\" cy=\"22.0\" r=\"13\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\" stroke=\"#FFFFFF\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"26.0\" y=\"27.0\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#FFFFFF\" text-anchor=\"middle\">4</text><text x=\"46.0\" y=\"28.0\" font-size=\"17\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\" text-anchor=\"start\">Dry everything. Oil lightly.</text><rect x=\"40.0\" y=\"90.0\" width=\"58.0\" height=\"58.0\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#FFFFFF\" stroke=\"#1F3D2B\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><circle cx=\"69.0\" cy=\"112.0\" r=\"8.8\" fill=\"#2E7D4F\" stroke=\"#FFFFFF\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><path d=\"M65.0 112.0 l3.2 3.2 l5.6 -6.4\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#FFFFFF\" stroke-width=\"2.5\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><text x=\"69.0\" y=\"140.0\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#17201A\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Bore</text><rect x=\"110.0\" y=\"90.0\" width=\"58.0\" height=\"58.0\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#FFFFFF\" stroke=\"#1F3D2B\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><circle cx=\"139.0\" cy=\"112.0\" r=\"8.8\" fill=\"#2E7D4F\" stroke=\"#FFFFFF\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><path d=\"M135.0 112.0 l3.2 3.2 l5.6 -6.4\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#FFFFFF\" stroke-width=\"2.5\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><text x=\"139.0\" y=\"140.0\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#17201A\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Bolt</text><rect x=\"180.0\" y=\"90.0\" width=\"58.0\" height=\"58.0\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#FFFFFF\" stroke=\"#1F3D2B\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><circle cx=\"209.0\" cy=\"112.0\" r=\"8.8\" fill=\"#2E7D4F\" stroke=\"#FFFFFF\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><path d=\"M205.0 112.0 l3.2 3.2 l5.6 -6.4\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#FFFFFF\" stroke-width=\"2.5\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><text x=\"209.0\" y=\"140.0\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#17201A\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Carrier</text><rect x=\"250.0\" y=\"90.0\" width=\"58.0\" height=\"58.0\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#FFFFFF\" stroke=\"#1F3D2B\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><circle cx=\"279.0\" cy=\"112.0\" r=\"8.8\" fill=\"#2E7D4F\" stroke=\"#FFFFFF\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><path d=\"M275.0 112.0 l3.2 3.2 l5.6 -6.4\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#FFFFFF\" stroke-width=\"2.5\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><text x=\"279.0\" y=\"140.0\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#17201A\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Piston</text><rect x=\"320.0\" y=\"90.0\" width=\"58.0\" height=\"58.0\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#FFFFFF\" stroke=\"#1F3D2B\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><circle cx=\"349.0\" cy=\"112.0\" r=\"8.8\" fill=\"#2E7D4F\" stroke=\"#FFFFFF\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><path d=\"M345.0 112.0 l3.2 3.2 l5.6 -6.4\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#FFFFFF\" stroke-width=\"2.5\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><text x=\"349.0\" y=\"140.0\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#17201A\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Tube</text><text x=\"200.0\" y=\"196.0\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#B3261E\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Water left inside rusts too.</text><text x=\"200.0\" y=\"218.0\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#17201A\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Dry fully, then a light oil coat.</text><text x=\"200.0\" y=\"240.0\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#17201A\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Run a patch again over the next days.</text>\n</svg>\n<figcaption><b>4.</b> Dry everything. Light oil.</figcaption></figure></div><div class=\"steps-nav\"><button class=\"steps-prev\" aria-label=\"Back\">‹ Back</button><span class=\"steps-dots\"><i></i><i></i><i></i><i></i></span><button class=\"steps-next\" aria-label=\"Next\">Next ›</button></div></div><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: the method and the sources</summary><ul><li>The manual's routine (95%, US Army TC 9-56): wet a patch with bore cleaner and run it through the bore several times; brush the bore and chamber several times; dry patches until clean; inspect; clean other parts and soak small parts; dry with clean rags; \"cover all parts with a light coat of oil\".</li><li>For corrosive salts, water based cleaning first (65%, AccurateShooter 2018). One method: window cleaner with ammonia or hot water through the bore and over the bolt, carrier and gas parts, scrub with a toothbrush, then dry fully and oil (60%, Paul Markel via AccurateShooter). Label: Tip.</li><li>Water left in the rifle also rusts. Dry everything, then oil <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">65%</span>.</li><li>Do it the same day. Run a dry patch again over the next few days and look for orange (Tip).</li><li>Do not forget the gas piston and tube: the hot gas carries residue there (Tip, owner advice).</li><li>Routine cleaning and oil choices are in <a href=\"#/s/firearm-care/0\">gun care</a>.</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"The SKS with its cleaning kit in orange: 1 the combination tool case in a trap in the butt, 2 the cleaning rod under the barrel.\">\n<rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#EEF1EA\"/>\n<text x=\"200.0\" y=\"26.0\" font-size=\"18\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\" text-anchor=\"middle\">The built in cleaning kit</text>\n<polygon points=\"10.0,124.9 10.0,173.2 32.3,165.8 97.4,142.7 121.6,133.1 188.6,131.6 233.2,127.9 292.7,122.6 295.0,118.2 292.7,114.5 195.3,114.5 195.3,115.6 117.9,115.6 114.2,118.2 99.3,120.0\" fill=\"#A8743F\" stroke=\"#6E4A2A\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/><rect x=\"11.5\" y=\"142.7\" width=\"8.2\" height=\"9.7\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#FF6A13\" stroke=\"#6E4A2A\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><polygon points=\"160.7,131.6 160.7,138.3 188.6,139.8 191.5,136.0 190.8,131.6\" fill=\"#59625C\" stroke=\"#17201A\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/><polygon points=\"158.1,132.3 160.3,132.3 159.5,139.0 157.7,139.0\" fill=\"#3A403C\" stroke=\"#17201A\" stroke-width=\"1.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/><path d=\"M132.8 132.3 L133.9 142.0 L155.8 142.0 L157.3 132.3\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#3A403C\" stroke-width=\"2.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/><path d=\"M146.9 132.3 Q144.7 136.0 146.2 139.8\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#3A403C\" stroke-width=\"2.5\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><line x1=\"138.3\" y1=\"133.4\" x2=\"143.9\" y2=\"136.4\" stroke=\"#3A403C\" stroke-width=\"3\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><circle cx=\"138.3\" cy=\"133.4\" r=\"2.0\" fill=\"#3A403C\" stroke=\"#17201A\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><polygon points=\"117.1,115.6 117.1,105.5 120.9,103.3 196.0,103.3 196.0,115.6\" fill=\"#59625C\" stroke=\"#17201A\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/><path d=\"M120.1 103.3 L121.6 100.0 Q158.8 98.5 196.0 100.0 L196.0 103.3 Z\" fill=\"#8E9690\" stroke=\"#17201A\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><line x1=\"120.9\" y1=\"107.8\" x2=\"123.8\" y2=\"113.7\" stroke=\"#3A403C\" stroke-width=\"2.5\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><circle cx=\"120.9\" cy=\"107.8\" r=\"2.5\" fill=\"#3A403C\" stroke=\"#17201A\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><line x1=\"184.8\" y1=\"106.3\" x2=\"184.8\" y2=\"109.3\" stroke=\"#3A403C\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><circle cx=\"184.8\" cy=\"107.8\" r=\"4.0\" fill=\"#C8CCC6\" stroke=\"#17201A\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><rect x=\"195.3\" y=\"101.1\" width=\"23.1\" height=\"11.9\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#59625C\" stroke=\"#17201A\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><polygon points=\"197.5,101.1 216.8,97.7 217.6,101.1\" fill=\"#3A403C\" stroke=\"#17201A\" stroke-width=\"1.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/><rect x=\"195.3\" y=\"107.4\" width=\"194.2\" height=\"5.2\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#3A403C\" stroke=\"#17201A\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><rect x=\"218.3\" y=\"101.8\" width=\"89.3\" height=\"4.8\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#59625C\" stroke=\"#17201A\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><rect x=\"219.1\" y=\"100.0\" width=\"72.9\" height=\"7.1\" rx=\"1.116\" fill=\"#A8743F\" stroke=\"#6E4A2A\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><line x1=\"216.8\" y1=\"105.5\" x2=\"213.9\" y2=\"110.7\" stroke=\"#3A403C\" stroke-width=\"2.5\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><circle cx=\"216.8\" cy=\"105.5\" r=\"2.5\" fill=\"#3A403C\" stroke=\"#17201A\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><polygon points=\"305.7,101.1 320.6,101.1 320.6,113.3 307.6,113.3\" fill=\"#59625C\" stroke=\"#17201A\" stroke-width=\"1.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/><line x1=\"296.4\" y1=\"117.8\" x2=\"379.0\" y2=\"117.8\" stroke=\"#FF6A13\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><circle cx=\"379.0\" cy=\"117.8\" r=\"2.0\" fill=\"#FF6A13\" stroke=\"#17201A\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><polygon points=\"270.4,114.8 366.4,114.1 366.4,116.3 270.4,115.6\" fill=\"#AEB4AE\" stroke=\"#17201A\" stroke-width=\"1.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/><rect x=\"364.1\" y=\"112.6\" width=\"8.2\" height=\"5.2\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#59625C\" stroke=\"#17201A\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><rect x=\"372.7\" y=\"106.3\" width=\"10.0\" height=\"6.7\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#59625C\" stroke=\"#17201A\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><rect x=\"376.4\" y=\"98.8\" width=\"2.6\" height=\"7.4\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#3A403C\" stroke=\"#17201A\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><path d=\"M374.6 105.5 Q375.5 94.4 377.5 94.4 Q379.5 94.4 380.9 105.5\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#3A403C\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><g data-tip=\"Butt trap|Press the cover in the butt plate: the combination tool case pops out.\"><line x1=\"15.6\" y1=\"147.2\" x2=\"40.0\" y2=\"200.0\" stroke=\"#17201A\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><circle cx=\"15.6\" cy=\"147.2\" r=\"3\" fill=\"#17201A\"/><circle cx=\"40.0\" cy=\"200.0\" r=\"11\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\" stroke=\"#FFFFFF\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"40.0\" y=\"205.0\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#FFFFFF\" text-anchor=\"middle\">1</text></g><g data-tip=\"Cleaning rod|Under the barrel. Unlock the bayonet, let it hang, free the rod head from the front sight base, pull it out.\"><line x1=\"344.8\" y1=\"117.8\" x2=\"300.0\" y2=\"200.0\" stroke=\"#17201A\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><circle cx=\"344.8\" cy=\"117.8\" r=\"3\" fill=\"#17201A\"/><circle cx=\"300.0\" cy=\"200.0\" r=\"11\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\" stroke=\"#FFFFFF\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"300.0\" y=\"205.0\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#FFFFFF\" text-anchor=\"middle\">2</text></g><circle cx=\"25.0\" cy=\"236.0\" r=\"10\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\" stroke=\"#FFFFFF\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"25.0\" y=\"241.0\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#FFFFFF\" text-anchor=\"middle\">1</text><text x=\"41.0\" y=\"241.0\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#17201A\" text-anchor=\"start\">Tool kit in the butt</text><circle cx=\"25.0\" cy=\"258.0\" r=\"10\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\" stroke=\"#FFFFFF\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"25.0\" y=\"263.0\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#FFFFFF\" text-anchor=\"middle\">2</text><text x=\"41.0\" y=\"263.0\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#17201A\" text-anchor=\"start\">Rod under the barrel</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>Tool kit in a trap in the butt. Rod under the barrel <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">95%</span>.</li><li>Unlock the bayonet to free the rod <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">95%</span>.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: the kit in the manual</summary><ul><li>\"Press in on the cover in the butt plate until the combination tool case is ejected. Unlock the bayonet, let it hang vertically, and after disengaging the head of the cleaning rod from the front sight base, pull the cleaning rod out of the rifle\" (95%, TC 9-56).</li><li>Kit: combination tool, sling, charger clips, oiler <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">95%</span>. When used as a rod guide, the tool case cap twists onto the front sight base <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">95%</span>.</li><li>Tip: a coated one piece rod and a bore guide are kinder to the bore than the steel army rod.</li></ul></details>","<aside class=\"callout rule\" role=\"note\"><div class=\"callout-t\">Grandpa's rule (wisdom, not law)</div><p>Grandpa's rule (wisdom): Shoot salt, wash with water, finish with oil. Same day.</p></aside><aside class=\"callout mistake\" role=\"note\"><div class=\"callout-t\">Common mistakes</div><ul><li>Oiling a corrosive bore without washing it first.</li><li>Cleaning the bore and forgetting the gas tube and piston.</li><li>Taking surplus full metal jacket rounds hunting.</li></ul></aside><aside class=\"callout field\" role=\"note\"><div class=\"callout-t\">Do this in the field</div><p>Pack a range kit: water spray bottle, patches, toothbrush, rag, oil. Clean before you drive home.</p></aside>","<ul><li>US Army, <a href=\"https://archive.org/download/gunmanual_sksmanual/sksmanual.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">TC 9-56 SKS Rifle, Simonov Type 56 (October 1969)</a>: cleaning, tool kit, read directly 2026-10-23 <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">95%</span></li><li>AccurateShooter Daily Bulletin, <a href=\"https://bulletin.accurateshooter.com/?p=54322\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">\"Tech Tip: Coping with Corrosive Ammo\"</a>, 3 March 2018 (with Brownells and Paul Markel), read 2026-10-23 <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">65%</span></li><li>Wikipedia, <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/SKS\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">SKS</a>, chrome lining, read 2026-10-23 <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">70%</span></li><li>BC Hunting and Trapping Regulations Synopsis 2026 to 2028, page 12, via the <a href=\"#/s/rb-legal-methods/0\">Rule Book</a> <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">99%</span></li></ul>"]